Z||000000||cscougar||11-15-1999||08:58 AM||||Does anyone have a wiring diagram, showing the engine harness wiring for a 2.8 V-6 and also the diagram for the many vacuum hoses under the intake phenum?<P>I am rebuilding a V-6 that had the top removed when I got it.  Just trying to get everything back where it belongs.<P>Ted||||reg||1
Z||000001||Carrolles||11-15-1999||11:41 AM||||Hi,<P>I just finished putting the wiring harness and vacuum harness on my new engine (85SE v-6 4spd).  I don't remember finding a complete diagram of the wiring or vacuum harnesses in the Helms manual.  I used notes that I took as I dismanteled it.  I'd be glad to help if I can.<P>Most of the wiring isn't hard.  The plugs are all different and will only fit a given item.  Routing is a bit of a pain though especially if you haven't seen it mounted where it is supposed to go in the first place.  Let me know what I can do for you.  There are a few pictures in Helms of the wiring at the starter, battery cables, distributor, throttle body, and thermostat housing.<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000002||cscougar||11-15-1999||02:33 PM||||The biggest problem is the mass of vacuum lines that are under the red plenum.  I am not sure where they all go.<P>Ted||||reg||1
